Subject: airoha: expose NPU RX policy and TDMA admission counters

A zero RX-PPE counter is ambiguous without separating policy misses from a
full TDMA ring. Extend the shared ABI with read-only per-band counters. The
firmware increments them only after secure MPDU validation, and the host
reports them beside the existing owned-token counters.

--- a/include/linux/soc/airoha/kite-datapath.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/airoha/kite-datapath.h
@@ -156,4 +156,5 @@
 	unsigned int tx_sent[2], tx_freed[2], tx_drop[2], tx_bad_done;
 	unsigned int rx_ppe[2], rx_host[2], rx_replay[2], rx_stale[2];
 	unsigned int rx_miss[2], rx_free[2], rx_unsupported[2], tx_aborted[2], reserved[1];
+	unsigned int rx_policy_hit[2], rx_policy_miss[2], rx_tdma_full[2];
 	struct kdp_sta sta[KDP_WCIDS];
